{%- set faqs = [
  ["How does SOC as a Service work?", "SOCaaS collects and analyzes security logs from connected systems and applications using technologies such as Security Information and Event Management (SIEM). Security alerts are investigated and prioritized so potential threats can be addressed through appropriate response procedures."],
  ["What services are included in SOCaaS?", "SOCaaS typically includes security event monitoring and threat detection alongside log analysis and incident investigation. Depending on the service scope, it may also include threat intelligence and vulnerability monitoring with security reporting and incident response support."],
  ["What is the difference between SOCaaS and a traditional SOC?", "A traditional SOC operates through an organization's internal security team and infrastructure, whereas SOCaaS provides security monitoring through an external service provider. SOCaaS can reduce the need for in-house resources while providing access to specialized security technologies and expertise."],
  ["Does SOCaaS provide 24/7 security monitoring?", "SOCaaS can provide 24/7 security monitoring depending on the provider's service model and agreed service-level agreement (SLA). Organizations should confirm monitoring hours and incident escalation procedures when selecting a SOCaaS provider."],
  ["How does SOCaaS help detect cyber threats?", "SOCaaS uses security analytics and log correlation alongside threat intelligence to identify suspicious behavior and potential indicators of compromise. This helps security teams investigate threats such as malware activity and unauthorized access attempts."],
  ["Can SOCaaS monitor cloud environments?", "Yes. SOCaaS can monitor security events across cloud platforms such as AWS and Microsoft Azure. Monitoring can cover cloud workloads and access activity alongside relevant configuration changes and suspicious network behavior."],
  ["Is SOCaaS suitable for small and medium-sized businesses?", "Yes. SOCaaS can help small and medium-sized businesses access security monitoring and threat detection without the cost of building a dedicated in-house SOC. The service scope can be aligned with the organization's infrastructure and security requirements."],
  ["What is the role of SIEM in SOC as a Service?", "Security Information and Event Management (SIEM) collects and correlates security logs from multiple sources to identify suspicious patterns. Within SOCaaS, SIEM supports centralized monitoring and alert investigation while improving visibility into potential security incidents."],
  ["How quickly can SOCaaS respond to a security incident?", "Response time depends on incident severity and the provider's agreed SLA. SOCaaS may support alert triage and incident investigation alongside containment recommendations, while specific response actions and escalation timelines depend on the service agreement."],
  ["Does SOCaaS help with security compliance?", "SOCaaS can support compliance activities by maintaining relevant security logs and incident records alongside monitoring reports. These deliverables may contribute to requirements associated with ISO 27001 and SOC 2, although SOCaaS alone does not establish compliance or certification."],
  ["Why choose CipherTrivia for SOC as a Service?", "CipherTrivia helps organizations improve security visibility through SOC as a Service (SOCaaS) capabilities that focus on continuous monitoring and threat detection alongside incident investigation and security reporting. Our approach supports proactive risk identification and informed remediation across enterprise networks and cloud environments."]
] %}

